<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44528" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">smīlax</span></b> , ăcis,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμῖλαξ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Bindweed</i>, <i>withwind</i>, <i>rough smilax</i>: Smilax aspera, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				35, 63, § 153</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 10, 49, §
			82</span></i>.—Hence Smilax personified, <i>a
				maiden who was changed into this herb</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
				283</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The yew-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				10, 20, § 51</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A kind of oak</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 6,
				8, § 19</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
